From c4e8847f9c3d0276fe534db8c0246760c26291b1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 05:48:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(tools): tool calls wait out a plugin force-reload instead
 of reading a half-empty registry [daveey]

Problem: tool_call answered "'tailnet_exec' is not a known tool name" for a
name tool_search had just returned (hub state.db message rows 1043880,
1063368, 1181058, 1181060; three sessions, 2026-11-10..12).

Why 1: the name was absent from the tool registry when the bridge resolved it
  (tools/tool_search_validation.py not_deferrable_error, last branch).
Why 2: a forced plugin rediscovery was in flight in that process: the rows
  are stamped 19:30:29 and 00:51:32/34, inside the hermes-sync.log
  "mods-reload ... desktop-serve:9147" windows 19:30:27-29 and 00:51:25-38.
Why 3: PluginManager.discover_and_load(force=True) unloads every plugin
  registration of the home (tools and guard hooks) and only then registers
  them again; that takes seconds.
Why 4: the pass holds the manager's discovery lock, but tool resolution and
  registry.dispatch never take it; the registry lock is per operation.
Root (happened): reload visibility is not atomic for registry readers.
Root (not caught): registry tests cover single-operation locking, none drives
  a tool call while a real force reload is between unload and re-register.
Recurrence: first fix for this cause; earlier tool_search fixes addressed
  wire aliases and schema validation.

Fix: tools/registry_reload.py marks a home as mid-reload for the length of the
forced pass. handle_function_call waits for the mark before resolving and
resolves again when a pass overlapped a bridge read or refusal;
registry.dispatch re-reads after a miss during a pass. Waiting happens before
any handler is invoked, so nothing runs twice. The reloading thread and the
loader workers that copy its context never wait, another home's pass is not
waited on, and the wait is bounded at 60 s.

Proof: tests/tools/test_registry_reload_barrier.py holds a real force reload
open inside register(); without the fix tool_call returns the exact error,
registry.dispatch "Unknown tool", tool_describe not_found (3 failed), with it
7 passed.
